From 44f90c76dd72a7c38267514e8e853a5238ed92a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xuxh1 <18172956238@163.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 11:08:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(rice): flood irrigated paddies a set number of days
 before sowing (candidate 25)

DEF_PADDY_FALLOW_FLOOD (days, 0 or less is off, default 0): an irrigated
paddy (PFT 62, flood or paddy method) that is not growing is bunded and
topped up by the paddy irrigation (C-32b: puddled layer saturated plus 50 mm
standing water) from this many days before its next sowing, first season or
the C-45 second season, so the soil is anoxic at planting. The water comes
through the irrigation supply and is counted in the irrigation totals; none
is pumped onto frozen ground. 366 or more keeps the whole fallow flooded
(winter-flooded paddy). Rainfed rice is left alone. Needs
DEF_PADDY_RICE_BUND.

The flag is set at the start of each time step (CalPaddyFallowFlood, from
CoLMMAIN) from the date, croplive and the sowing dates only, so the
hydrology of the same step sees it and a restart gives the same flag.

Pre-season flooding of more than 30 d scales paddy emissions by 2.41 (SFp,
IPCC 2019 Refinement Vol. 4 Table 5.13); winter-drained fields emit 42 %
less in the rice season than winter-flooded ones (Cai et al. 2003); the
non-growing season is 24 % of the annual paddy emission in DLEM.

